## 🎨 CSS‑rotating card (hover)

Below is a **self‑contained** example – just copy the HTML and CSS into a file (or into an online editor like CodePen) and you’ll see a card that flips when you hover over it.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Obracająca się karta</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Wrapper – gives perspective ----------------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* creates 3‑D space */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card – the element that actually flips ----- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3‑D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth animation */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Hover – flip the card --------------------- */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* rotate around Y‑axis */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Front & Back faces ------------------------ */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the back side when turned */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card-front {
  background: #ff9a9e;          /* front colour */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
}

.card-back {
  background: #fad0c4;          /* back colour */
  transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* start flipped so it becomes visible on hover */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #333;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper | Gives depth to the 3‑D transform. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on `.card` | Keeps child elements (`.card-face`) in 3‑D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away. |
| **4** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Rotates the whole card 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| **5** | `transition` | Smoothly animates the rotation. |

Feel free to tweak colors, sizes, or use `rotateX` instead of `rotateY` for a vertical flip. Happy coding!
